  }
 },
 {
  "scene": "s01",
  "start": 58.853,
  "text": "To solve this mystery, we must reframe how we imagine cosmic space and time.",
  "sentences": [
   "s01.09"
  ],
  "id": "v013",
  "end": 65.229,
  "seconds": 6.38,
  "scene_start": false,
  "kind": "photo",
  "photo_subject": "a spiral galaxy",
  "photo_queries": [
   "spiral galaxy",
   "Andromeda galaxy"
  ],
  "card": {
   "type": "title",
   "title": "Reframing Space and Time"
  }
 },
 {
  "scene": "s02",
  "start": 65.229,
  "text": "Many people visualize the universe as a huge empty room where galaxies rocket through a dark void.",
  "sentences": [
   "s02.01"
  ],
  "id": "v014",
  "end": 72.106,
  "seconds": 6.88,
  "scene_start": true,
  "kind": "card",
  "card": {
   "type": "title",
   "title": "The False Picture of Galaxies Flying Through Empty Space"
  }
 },
 {
  "scene": "s02",
  "start": 72.106,
  "text": "In that false mental picture, galaxies are racing through a fixed, static space like cosmic shrapnel.",
  "sentences": [
   "s02.02"
  ],
  "id": "v015",
  "end": 78.969,
  "seconds": 6.86,
  "scene_start": false,
  "kind": "drawing",
  "drawing_subject": "galaxies flying through an empty dark room",
  "card": {
   "type": "title",
   "title": "Static Space Myth"
  }
 },
 {
  "scene": "s02",
  "start": 78.969,
  "text": "If that picture were correct, nothing could ever appear farther away than 13.8 billion light-years.",
  "sentences": [
   "s02.03"
  ],
  "id": "v016",
  "end": 86.28,
  "seconds": 7.31,
  "scene_start": false,
  "kind": "card",
  "card": {
   "type": "stat",
   "title": "Maximum Distance Limit",
   "value": "13.8 billion",
   "unit": "light-years"
  }
 },
 {
  "scene": "s02",
  "start": 86.28,
  "text": "But this common picture of cosmic expansion is completely wrong.",
  "sentences": [
   "s02.04"
  ],
  "id": "v017",
  "end": 91.713,
  "seconds": 5.43,
  "scene_start": false,
  "kind": "photo",
  "photo_subject": "a cluster of galaxies",
  "photo_queries": [
   "galaxy cluster",
   "Coma cluster"
  ],
  "card": {
   "type": "title",
   "title": "Expanding Universe"
  }
 },
 {
  "scene": "s02",
  "start": 91.713,
  "text": "Cosmic expansion is not galaxies moving through a pre-existing empty space.",
  "sentences": [
   "s02.05"
  ],
  "id": "v018",
  "end": 97.326,
  "seconds": 5.61,
  "scene_start": false,
  "kind": "drawing",
  "drawing_subject": "two galaxies drifting apart as space expands between them",
  "card": {
   "type": "title",
   "title": "Not Moving Through Space"
  }
 },
 {
  "scene": "s02",
  "start": 97.326,
  "text": "Instead, general relativity describes expansion as an intrinsic",
  "sentences": [
   "s02.06"
  ],
  "id": "v019",
  "end": 101.55449999999999,
  "seconds": 4.23,
  "scene_start": false,
  "kind": "photo",
  "photo_subject": "Albert Einstein",
  "photo_queries": [
   "Albert Einstein",
   "general relativity"
  ],
  "card": {
   "type": "title",
   "title": "General Relativity"
  }
 },
 {
  "scene": "s02",
  "start": 101.55449999999999,
  "text": "increase in distance between cosmic objects over time.",
  "sentences": [
   "s02.06"
  ],
  "id": "v020",
  "end": 106.257,
  "seconds": 4.7,
  "scene_start": false,
  "kind": "drawing",
  "drawing_subject": "a grid expanding in size over time",
  "card": {
   "type": "title",
   "title": "Increase in Distance"
  }
 },
 {
  "scene": "s02",
  "start": 106.257,
  "text": "Most galaxies are nearly at rest relative to their local comoving spatial coordinates.",
  "sentences": [
   "s02.07"
  ],
  "id": "v021",
  "end": 112.299,
  "seconds": 6.04,
  "scene_start": false,
  "kind": "photo",
  "photo_subject": "a distant star cluster",
  "photo_queries": [
   "star cluster",
   "globular cluster"
  ],
  "card": {
   "type": "title",
   "title": "Comoving Coordinates"
  }
 },
 {
  "scene": "s02",
  "start": 112.299,
  "text": "The velocity of a galaxy relative to its local comoving grid is called its peculiar velocity.",
  "sentences": [
   "s02.08"
  ],
  "id": "v022",
  "end": 118.942,
  "seconds": 6.64,
  "scene_start": false,
  "kind": "drawing",
  "drawing_subject": "a single galaxy with a velocity vector arrow",
  "card": {
   "type": "title",
   "title": "Peculiar Velocity"
  }
 },
 {
  "scene": "s02",
  "start": 118.942,
  "text": "These local peculiar velocities are caused mostly by gravity and are usually quite small.",
  "sentences": [
   "s02.09"
  ],
  "id": "v023",
  "end": 125.192,
  "seconds": 6.25,
  "scene_start": false,
  "kind": "photo",
  "photo_subject": "interacting galaxies",
  "photo_queries": [
   "interacting galaxies",
   "colliding galaxies"
  ],
  "card": {
   "type": "title",
   "title": "Gravity Effects"
  }
 },
 {
  "scene": "s02",
  "start": 125.192,
  "text": "So how should we picture the movement of galaxies as the universe expands?",
  "sentences": [
   "s02.10"
  ],
  "id": "v024",
  "end": 130.234,
  "seconds": 5.04,
  "scene_start": false,
  "kind": "drawing",
  "drawing_subject": "a galaxy surrounded by expanding space lines",
  "card": {
   "type": "title",
   "title": "Galaxy Movement"
  }
 },
 {
  "scene": "s02",
  "start": 130.234,
  "text": "Understanding this key distinction changes everything about how we calculate cosmic distances.",
  "sentences": [
   "s02.12"
  ],
  "id": "v025",
  "end": 137.513,
  "seconds": 7.28,
  "scene_start": false,
  "kind": "card",
  "card": {
   "type": "flow",
   "title": "Cosmic Distances",
   "steps": [
    "Identify coordinates",
    "Measure expansion",
    "Calculate true distance"
   ]
  }
 },
 {
  "scene": "s03",
  "start": 137.513,
  "text": "To understand cosmic distances, imagine space as an",
  "sentences": [
   "s03.01"
  ],
  "id": "v026",
  "end": 141.21166666666667,
  "seconds": 3.7,
  "scene_start": true,
  "kind": "card",
  "card": {
   "type": "title",
   "title": "Space as an Expanding Fabric Rather Than a Static Box"
  }
 },
 {
  "scene": "s03",
  "start": 141.21166666666667,
  "text": "expanding fabric rather than a rigid stage.",
